title: The biggest
golf: 12

Write `biggest(nums)` that returns the largest number in a list.
Watch out: the numbers can be negative.
=== starter
def biggest(nums):
    ...
=== broken
def biggest(nums):
    best = 0
    for n in nums:
        if n > best:
            best = n
    return best
=== test
from harness import eq


def test_biggest(sol):
    eq(sol.biggest([3, 9, 2]), 9, "biggest([3, 9, 2])")
    eq(sol.biggest([-5, -2, -8]), -2, "biggest([-5, -2, -8])")
